WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.701
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.133
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.234
You are here.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.300
You made it.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.067
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:08.067
Thank you very much.
Well, guys,

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.334
this will put you
in a good mood.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.234
I want to say congrats
to our good friends,

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.868
Jennifer Lopez and Ben Affleck,
who got married

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.100
over the weekend in Las Vegas.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.834
[ Rimshot ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.234
And they're great.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.968
That's right, they got married
at a drive-through chapel.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.934
You know inflation's bad
when even those two are like,

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.400
"Let's just do it in Vegas.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.467
[ Laughter ]
Let's just go to Vegas."

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:31.367
The guy who married them
was like,

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:32.534
"Wow, you two are the best

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:34.934
Ben and J.Lo impersonators
I've ever seen.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.501
[ Laughter ]
You're really good."

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.734
Yeah, they got married
at a drive-through chapel,

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.501
which was a compromise
because Jen wanted

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.868
to get married at a chapel
and Ben wanted to get married

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.200
at a Dunkin' Donuts
drive-through.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.834
[ Laughter ]
It's like it's very Boston.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.734
It's a Boston thing.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:50.100
I saw that J.Lo is
taking Ben's last name

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.234
and will now go
by Jennifer Affleck.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:53.267
[ Murmuring ]

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.501
That's good.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.167
Because, if she went
by Jennifer Lopez Affleck,

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.601
her nickname would be J.LoAf.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:01.667
Not as cute.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.567
Ever since the news came out
about Jennifer Lopez

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:04.767
and Ben Affleck's
surprise wedding,

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.467
a lot of people have been saying
the whole story

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:08.667
reminds them
of the plot of a J.Lo movie.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.167
-I've been saying that all day.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.501
-Oh, yeah?
What's that, Tariq?

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.367
-Well, you know,
this whole thing is just like

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:16.400
that J.Lo movie where, you know,
she makes the guy

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.400
who was holding up that sign,
you know, she marries him.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.133
-Yeah, you mean "Marry Me"?

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.334
-No, no, no, not "Marry Me."

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.267
The one where she marries
the guy who saves her

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:28.534
from being crushed by --
it was like a runaway Dumpster.

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:30.100
-You mean "The Wedding Planner?"

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.734
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:35.334
I mean, the one where she falls
for the hunky Senate candidate

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.033
who's staying
at the hotel where she works.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.267
-"Maid in Manhattan"?

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:40.434
-No, no, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.200
I'm talking about --
I'm talking about the one

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.367
where her mother-in-law,
she wears the white dress

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.601
to her wedding,
instead of the peach-colored one

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.901
that J.Lo asked her to, so.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.634
"Monster-in-Law."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:53.267
-Jimmy, have you ever even seen
a J.Lo movie?

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.133
It's the one
where she and her friends,

00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:00.334
they commit credit fraud,
you know, in fur coats.

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:03.100
-"Hustlers"?
-No, no, no, not "Hustlers," no.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.801
[ Laughter ]
The one where, you know,
she's a real estate agent

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.167
and she figures out

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:10.100
that Jason Statham is
a jewel thief.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.868
-"Parker"?
-Come on, man!

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:13.667
[ Laughter ]
You know the one!

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:16.234
Look, man, she's a female
saber-toothed tiger,

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.400
forced to join
a band of pirates.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.434
-"Ice Age: Continental Drift"?
-No!

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.567
[ Laughter ]
No!

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.000
The one where her new student
becomes obsessed with her

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.567
and then they have
that big showdown in the barn.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:30.033
-"The Boy Next Door"?

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.767
-Jimmy, look, it's the one where

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.767
[ Laughter ]
she uses VR to travel

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.868
inside the mind of a psychopath,

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:39.133
in order to save
his latest victim.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:40.267
-"The Cell"?

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:43.734
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.934
The one where she teams up
with Ice Cube, you know,

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:47.534
to fight an anaconda.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:48.968
-"Anaconda"!

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.334
-Yeah, "Anaconda," that's it.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:53.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:54.000
What does --

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.133
How does a surprise wedding
in Las Vegas

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.534
remind you of "Anaconda"?

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:01.734
-Well, was Jon Voight there?

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:02.934
-No.

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:04.334
-Oh, well, never mind.

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Moving on.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.400
Let's get to some news --
on Friday, President Biden held

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.901
a controversial meeting with the
crown prince of Saudi Arabia.

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.467
But the real controversy was
that Biden greeted him

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.701
with a fist bump.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.200
Watch this.
Watch this.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:29.133
-Ooh.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:30.167
-Yeah.

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:31.534
Biden said,
"That wasn't a fist bump.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.667
That was me trying to punch him
as hard as I could."

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:36.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:39.834
[ Indistinct ]

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.701
Not a great look.
That's like a greeting Putin

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:43.167
with a chest bump and a bro hug.

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.501
"My man! What are you doing?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:48.300
Meanwhile, I read that Dr. Fauci
said that he plans to retire

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.434
by the end
of President Biden's term.

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:52.701
Yep, then everyone turn
to Biden like,

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.934
"Is there anything you'd like
to announce, too?"

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.667
Of course, once he's gone,
Fauci will be replaced

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.567
by a new,
slightly weaker, variant.

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.000
[ Laughter and ohhs ]

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.968
Guys listen to this --
according to a recent study,

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:10.234
COVID can live on frozen meat
for more than a month.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.601
I feel bad for the scientists

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:13.901
who spent a month rubbing
nasal swabs on frozen meat.

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:16.267
[ Laughter ]
Seriously, you know we're living

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:18.167
in fun times
when you're giving your sausage

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.767
a PCR test, you know?

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.868
[ The Roots play funk sting ]

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:25.734
-Sausage.
-Oh.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:26.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:27.934
Meanwhile, Arby's was like,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.400
"This doesn't apply to us

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.567
because our meat is stored
at room temperature."

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:35.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.234
Some business news --
there's a new lawsuit

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:39.767
against Skittles
that claims that it contained

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:44.167
a known toxin called
titanium dioxide.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.634
Well, Skittles wants
to assure people

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:47.767
that their candy is safe
and toxin-free,

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:50.100
but I think the new ad
went a little too far.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.300
Watch this.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.334
-Here at Skittles,

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.300
we want to set
the record straight.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.667
We don't use harmful toxins

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.133
because all of our candy is...

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:01.434
Each and every Skittle is...

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:05.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:07.968
Then, of course,
all Skittles are...

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:09.334
[ Thwack ]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.400
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.133
-It's the heart.
-Farmer Skitty.

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.501
Guys, you know,
I was thinking about this.

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:21.934
I saw this today -- in TikTok,

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:25.033
their head of global security
just stepped down, yeah.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.634
And he actually released a video
announcing his resignation

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:30.067
that was pretty on-brand
for Tik-Tok.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:31.033
Check this out.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.467
-Effective September 2nd,

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:33.567
I will be stepping down

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:35.501
as TikTok's
chief security officer.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.834
-♪ My money don't
jiggle-jiggle ♪

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:41.968
[ Laughter ]
♪ It folds ♪

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:43.400
♪ I like to see you
wiggle-wiggle ♪

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.267
♪ For sure ♪

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:45.901
[ Applause ]
And he left.

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.434
That's how he resigned.

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:48.934
Yeah, that's how he resigned.

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.267
Well, this is cool --

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:51.734
are you guys fans
of the game Wordle?

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:52.434
You ever play Wordle?

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:53.567
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:54.901
Good.

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:57.200
Well, I saw that Hasbro
and The New York Times

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.467
are creating a new Wordle
board game.

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:00.601
[ Oohs ]

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:02.601
It's called
Wordle: The Party Game.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:05.000
-Oh.
-We actually got a sneak peek

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:05.701
at the instructions.

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:06.434
Take a look at this.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:07.267
Step...

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.934 --> 00:06:10.801
Step...

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:14.934
Step...

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:17.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:19.067
And, finally, Step...

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:24.434
[ Laughter and applause ]
[ Sad trombone ]

00:06:24.434 --> 00:06:25.767
-[Both] Party!

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:27.234
♪ Wordle party ♪

00:06:27.234 --> 00:06:29.067
-♪ And Wordle ♪
-♪ Wordle party ♪

00:06:29.067 --> 00:06:31.000
-♪ And Wordle ♪
-♪ Wordle party ♪

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.701
-♪ And Wordle and party ♪

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:33.567
♪ And Wordle ♪

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:34.601
-Wordle.

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:35.334
Wordle.

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:38.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:41.667
Hey, guys, I heard that 7-Eleven
gave seven years of free coffee

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.400
to the parents of a baby born

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.701
in one of their parking lots
in West Virginia.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:48.434
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, and now the baby is
one week old,

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:49.767
just like the hot dogs.
-Oh.

00:06:49.767 --> 00:06:50.634
[ Laughter ]

